Comment:
 The bundled Bible database (/usr/share/leverbe/bible.db) is built from
 public-domain and openly licensed texts: KJV with Strong's (bolls.life),
 unfoldingWord Literal Text (CC BY-SA 4.0), Louis Segond 1910, the Westminster
 Leningrad Codex / OpenScriptures morphhb (CC BY 4.0), SBLGNT / MorphGNT
 (CC BY-SA), the Septuagint and Vulgata Clementina (getbible.net), and the
 OpenScriptures Strong's lexicons. See the project README for details.

Offline study library:
 Matthew Henry (complete/unabridged), John Calvin, Albert Barnes, Adam Clarke,
 Jamieson–Fausset–Brown, and Treasury of Scripture Knowledge:
 public-domain SWORD modules distributed by CrossWire (www.crosswire.org).
 Original module configurations and acknowledgements are preserved in
 /usr/share/doc/leverbe-parallel/study-sources.json.
 Matthew Poole: Annotations upon the Holy Bible, 1688, volumes I–II.
 J. C. Ryle: Expository Thoughts on the Gospels, seven historical volumes.
 John Owen: Exposition of Hebrews, Thomas Tegg, 1840, four volumes.
 These historical public-domain editions are scan OCR from Internet Archive
 and contributing libraries. Scan and Google digitization credits are retained.
 OCR is uncorrected and may contain errors. Exact sources, editions and download
 checksums are recorded in study-sources.json. The application is not affiliated
 with Bible Gateway, Blue Letter Bible, CrossWire or Internet Archive.
